  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Pentosan polysulfate sodium is a heparin-like drug used as an anticoagulant and, in urology, to treat bladder conditions such as interstitial cystitis. It is an approved medicine, used mainly in urological care, and is also being studied for other conditions.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7165276&quot;>Wikidata Q7165276</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>pentosan polysulfate sodium</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>C05BA04, G04BX15</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00686&quot;>DB00686</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/37720&quot;>37720</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:184555&quot;>184555</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7165276&quot;>Q7165276</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C10H18O21S4</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>602.473 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
